{
 "_notes": [
  "Discogs genres for the canonical genre: vocabulary (TAG-077, TAG-078, ADR-0023, ADR-0030). Keys starting with _ are comments. Terminology (ADR-0030): every node below level 1 is a genre; level 1 is a family. Discogs calls its level-1 names genres and its finer names styles; here its genres are the families and its styles are genres.",
  "families: the Discogs level-1 names kept (11 of the 15; Brass & Military, Children's, Non-Music and Stage & Screen are removed) in the fixed order of GEN-037. genres: lowercase genre name to its parents, a list of families: parents[0] is the family Discogs files it under (the first in the GEN-037 order, or a reviewed override: disco, new wave, acid jazz, gospel, rhythm and blues, dub and the older overrides of ADR-0021); any further entry is another family Discogs also files it under (GEN-039).",
  "Spelling: the name is Discogs's lowercased, except where the project already used another spelling (drum and bass, rock and roll, rhythm and blues, psytrance, synthpop, hi-nrg, hip house, euro disco, dance pop and the like): lookups ignore case, spaces, hyphens and '&' versus 'and', and one spelling is stored. discogs_names lists the names that differ beyond that.",
  "Source: the Discogs genres and styles list (support.discogs.com help article, Database Guidelines, Genres and Styles). Only names and the relation of a Discogs style to its Discogs genre are used, no release data. The article is behind a bot check, so the list was written from memory of it and each name was checked against the public Discogs database search (the style=<name> query parameter, no token, 2026-10-16): a name is kept when releases with exactly that Discogs style exist. The relation of a name to its family cannot be read from the search (Discogs genre and style filter independently), so it comes from the reviewed table of ADR-0021 and the Discogs list as remembered; see README.md.",
  "unverified: names kept without a successful search check (see README.md); empty means every name was found in the Discogs database.",
  "Electronic is now the temporary group Others (task-0066, 2026-10-20): it still lists as a family here but is not a vocabulary entry (a group is never assigned to a song)."
 ],
